  "result": "Perfect! All 115 tests are passing. Let me verify the VAT implementation is complete:\n\n**Summary of VAT Implementation:**\n\n1. **Added `lineVAT()` function** that:\n   - Calculates VAT on the line amount AFTER applying the discount\n   - Formula: `(line_total - line_discount) * vatRate / 100`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` for proper rounding\n   - Clamps result to minimum 0\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return** `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n   - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals\n   - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n   - `vat` = sum of all line VATs (rounded per line)\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText()`** to show:\n   - Line items with quantities, names, unit prices, and totals\n   - Subtotal\n   - Discount line (only if discount > 0)\n   - VAT line\n   - Total\n\n4. **Added 9 new VAT tests** covering:\n   - VAT calculation with different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - VAT calculated after discount\n   - Mixed VAT rates on single invoice\n   - VAT with tier discounts\n   - VAT with explicit discounts\n\nThe implementation correctly handles:\n- Per-line VAT calculation after discount\n- Multiple VAT rates on same invoice\n- Proper rounding per line (never at invoice level)\n- Clamping to prevent negative amounts\n- Integration with tier discounts and line discounts",
